From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dov Slansky <dslansky@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] harness-device: tap the face to answer an agent's question

The question review screen (question.read / answer.reviewed) had no way in from
the Focus face: a touch always started voice. Now, when the agent on the face
has an open question and the daemon serves question.review, the touch opens
that question so it can be answered on the glass. Everything else is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/devices/harness-device/firmware/main/ui/habitat/ui_habitat.c b/devices/harness-device/firmware/main/ui/habitat/ui_habitat.c
index 50b4f1f1f..8f066e825 100644
--- a/devices/harness-device/firmware/main/ui/habitat/ui_habitat.c
+++ b/devices/harness-device/firmware/main/ui/habitat/ui_habitat.c
@@ -3808,7 +3808,13 @@ void habitat_touch(bool down, int x, int y, uint32_t now)
              * and let go before the 650 ms that opens the tabs.
              */
             ht_gesture_guard(&gesture, now);
-            if (s.connected && !s.loading && (active() || swarm_mode())) {
+            if (s.connected && !s.loading && !swarm_mode() && active() && is_question(active()->id) &&
+                cable_client_supports(CABLE_FEATURE_QUESTIONS)) {
+                // An agent waiting on its question: the touch opens the question to answer on the
+                // glass, from a daemon that serves question.review. Otherwise the face talks, as before.
+                ESP_LOGI("habitat", "focus touch: open question");
+                open_question();
+            } else if (s.connected && !s.loading && (active() || swarm_mode())) {
                 ESP_LOGI("habitat", "focus touch: start voice");
                 // Built as the old microphone's was: make_action names the agent on the face, and
                 // main-surface voice without a recipient is dropped.
